@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pru-nouns`
IMPORT `pru-fixtures`
IMPORT `pru-general`
IMPORT `pru-annex`
IMPORT `pru-exclusions`
IMPORT `pru-benefits`
IMPORT `pru-claims`
IMPORT `pru-contract`
IMPORT `pru-notes`

-- The evidence for NOTES.md section 4, Findings. Each assertion states what the source, as
-- encoded, answers in a case that exposes a defect or a disagreement between the summary
-- notes and the Rules and Terms. They are expected to pass: a finding is that the answer is
-- surprising, not that the encoding misreads it. Expected values were worked by hand from the
-- source before running, as in pru-tests.l4.

§ `Findings`

§§ `F-01 — an accidental death after day 180 is paid by no Article`

-- Day 181 from an Accident with no excluded cause: nothing (8.1 needs 180 days; 8.7 needs a
-- death not caused by an Accident).
#ASSERT `the death claim` `the policy` (`a death on` ((YMD 2027 3 10) PLUS 181) `from` (JUST `the accident`) `as` `any other circumstance`) `the accounts` `nothing paid yet` EQUALS `no Article of the Rules and Terms pays for this death`
-- The same death, had the insured been under an unprescribed substance (excluded, 11.1(e)):
-- 11.2 has no 180-day limit and pays the premiums, 30m.
#ASSERT `the death claim` `the policy` (`a death on` ((YMD 2027 3 10) PLUS 181) `from` (JUST (`an accident on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `with` (`a substance, linked as` `directly caused by it` `prescribed` FALSE `and the cause of the Accident` TRUE))) `as` `any other circumstance`) `the accounts` `nothing paid yet` EQUALS `the excluded-death payment, Article 11.2` 30_000_000
-- And a death from illness the same day: 8.7, 30m.
#ASSERT `the death claim` `the policy` (`a death on` ((YMD 2027 3 10) PLUS 181) `from` NOTHING `as` `any other circumstance`) `the accounts` `nothing paid yet` EQUALS `the non-accidental death benefit, Article 8.7` 30_000_000

§§ `F-02 — claiming the permanent-injury maximum forfeits the death benefit`

-- Both legs lost on 2027-03-10: 100%, the 8.2 maximum, paid 2027-04-01; 8.2 and Article 16
-- end the contract on that payment.
#ASSERT `Article 8.2 — the permanent-injury benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (LIST `loss of both legs`) (YMD 2027 3 10) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 1_000_000_000
#ASSERT `Article 8.2 — the contract ends with this payment` `the policy` 1_000_000_000 `nothing paid yet`
#ASSERT `Article 16 — the date the contract terminates` `the policy` (`The termination events` OF NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, JUST (YMD 2027 4 1), NOTHING) EQUALS YMD 2027 4 1
-- The insured dies of the same Accident on day 40 (2027-04-19), within 180 days: the contract
-- is no longer in force, so 8.1 pays nothing. Without the 8.2 claim, 8.1 pays 1bn, of which
-- 8.10 would deduct nothing (day 40 is after day 30).
#ASSERT `the death claim` (`the policy, lapsed on` (YMD 2027 4 1) `and reinstated on` NOTHING) (`a death on` ((YMD 2027 3 10) PLUS 40) `from` (JUST `the accident`) `as` `any other circumstance`) `the accounts` `nothing paid yet` EQUALS `nothing, because the contract was not in force at the death`
#ASSERT `the death claim` `the policy` (`a death on` ((YMD 2027 3 10) PLUS 40) `from` (JUST `the accident`) `as` `any other circumstance`) `the accounts` `nothing paid yet` EQUALS `the accidental death benefit, Article 8.1` 1_000_000_000

§§ `F-03 — accidental blindness and accidental paralysis fall between 8.2 and 8.8`

-- Total blindness in both eyes, eyeballs intact: section 1 lists only the loss of the eyeball.
#ASSERT `Article 8.2 — the permanent-injury benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (LIST `an injury the table does not list` "total blindness in both eyes, eyeballs intact") (YMD 2027 3 10) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays nothing, because` `the injury is not one the payout-rate table lists`
-- Yet Article 1.17 counts total blindness as loss of an eye, so the same blindness from illness
-- is a total and permanent disability, paid under 8.8 (30m); from an Accident, 8.8 refuses.
#ASSERT `Article 8.8 — the disability benefit` `the policy` (`a disability of` (JUST `both eyes`) `by paralysis` FALSE `capacity lost` NOTHING `from` (YMD 2027 3 10) `certified` (YMD 2027 3 20)) NOTHING `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 30_000_000
#ASSERT `Article 8.8 — the disability benefit` `the policy` (`a disability of` (JUST `both eyes`) `by paralysis` FALSE `capacity lost` NOTHING `from` (YMD 2027 3 10) `certified` (YMD 2027 3 20)) (JUST `the accident`) `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays nothing, because` `the disability was caused by an Accident`
-- Paraplegia from a road accident: no row of section 1, and 8.8 refuses because it was an Accident.
#ASSERT `Article 8.2 — the permanent-injury benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (LIST `an injury the table does not list` "complete paralysis of both legs") (YMD 2027 3 10) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays nothing, because` `the injury is not one the payout-rate table lists`
#ASSERT `Article 8.8 — the disability benefit` `the policy` (`a disability of` (JUST `both legs`) `by paralysis` TRUE `capacity lost` NOTHING `from` (YMD 2027 3 10) `certified` (YMD 2027 9 10)) (JUST `the accident`) `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays nothing, because` `the disability was caused by an Accident`

§§ `F-04 — the fingers of one hand: the parts are worth more than the whole`

-- "all the fingers of one hand" is 25% (250m); the same loss itemised, a thumb (15%) and four
-- fingers (5% each), is 35% (350m), and 8.2 adds the rates of several injuries.
#ASSERT `Article 8.2 — the permanent-injury benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (LIST `loss of all the fingers of one hand`) (YMD 2027 3 10) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 250_000_000
#ASSERT `Article 8.2 — the permanent-injury benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (LIST `loss of one thumb`, `loss of one finger`, `loss of one finger`, `loss of one finger`, `loss of one finger`) (YMD 2027 3 10) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 350_000_000

§§ `F-05 — the youngest band's cap has no VND ceiling`

-- Sum insured 2bn, events on 2027-03-10: aged 5, 50% = 1bn; aged 10, the lesser of 2bn and
-- 250m; aged 30, the lesser of 2bn and 500m. A 5-year-old's cap is four times a 10-year-old's
-- and twice an adult's.
#ASSERT `the term cap for fractures and burns, for` (`the same policy for` 2_000_000_000 `on an insured born` (YMD 2021 6 1)) `at an event on` (YMD 2027 3 10) EQUALS 1_000_000_000
#ASSERT `the term cap for fractures and burns, for` (`the same policy for` 2_000_000_000 `on an insured born` (YMD 2016 6 1)) `at an event on` (YMD 2027 3 10) EQUALS 250_000_000
#ASSERT `the term cap for fractures and burns, for` (`the same policy for` 2_000_000_000 `on an insured born` (YMD 1996 6 1)) `at an event on` (YMD 2027 3 10) EQUALS 500_000_000

§§ `F-06 — an ankle fracture is also a fracture of the tibia or fibula`

-- One break, two rows: "the ankle" 15% (150m) or "one or more leg bones ... tibia, fibula"
-- 30% (300m). Which row is a classification the Rules and Terms do not settle.
#ASSERT `Article 8.4 — the fracture benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (LIST `a fracture of` `the ankle` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `previously broken` NOTHING) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 150_000_000
#ASSERT `Article 8.4 — the fracture benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (LIST `a fracture of` `one or more leg bones: femur, patella, tibia, fibula` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `previously broken` NOTHING) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 300_000_000

§§ `F-07 — overlapping rows: kidneys, and burns of mixed degree`

-- Both kidneys injured: two "kidney injury" rows (5% each) and the "both kidneys" row (10%)
-- all describe it; read literally and added under 8.3, 20% (200m) rather than 10%.
#ASSERT `Article 8.3 — the internal-organ benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (LIST `kidney injury with one of the listed conditions`, `kidney injury with one of the listed conditions`, `injury to both kidneys in the same Accident`) (YMD 2027 3 10) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 200_000_000
-- 10% at third degree and 12% at second (22% burned at second degree or worse): the 25% row
-- under fork F-07; the 50% row if third-degree area also counts as "phỏng độ 2".
#ASSERT `the table rate for the burn` (`a burn of` 10 `percent at third degree and` 12 `percent at second degree`) EQUALS 25%

§§ `F-08 — a deadline that can fall before the event it needs documents for`

-- 8.6 pays for a hospital transfer with no time limit after the Accident; 10.5 wants the
-- transfer paper within 60 days of the Accident. A transfer on day 70 cannot meet it.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 10.5 — the transfer paper can exist before the deadline` (YMD 2027 3 10) ((YMD 2027 3 10) PLUS 70)
#ASSERT `Article 8.6 — the ambulance benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (`treated overnight in` NOTHING `transferred` TRUE) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 1_000_000

§§ `F-09 — temporary cover`

-- War is not among Article 3's exclusions: a death in a riot during temporary cover pays 200m;
-- the same death after the certificate issues is excluded (11.1(a)) and gets 11.2's 30m.
#ASSERT `Article 3 — what is paid on a death during temporary cover` (`The temporary cover` OF (YMD 2026 1 2), JUST (YMD 2026 1 15), 1_000_000_000) (`a death on` (YMD 2026 1 10) `from` (JUST (`an accident on` (YMD 2026 1 9) `with` (`war, linked as` `directly caused by it`))) `as` `any other circumstance`) `the accounts` EQUALS `the temporary cover benefit` 200_000_000
#ASSERT `the death claim` `the policy` (`a death on` (YMD 2027 3 20) `from` (JUST (`an accident on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `with` (`war, linked as` `directly caused by it`))) `as` `any other circumstance`) `the accounts` `nothing paid yet` EQUALS `the excluded-death payment, Article 11.2` 30_000_000
-- The refund threshold is 200m of premium, not the benefit: premiums of 150m against a sum
-- insured of 100m give a benefit of 100m and no refund, less than was paid in.
#ASSERT `Article 3 — what is paid on a death during temporary cover` (`The temporary cover` OF (YMD 2026 1 2), JUST (YMD 2026 1 15), 100_000_000) (`a death on` (YMD 2026 1 10) `from` (JUST (`an accident on` (YMD 2026 1 9) `with` `no excluded cause`)) `as` `any other circumstance`) (`accounts with premiums` 150_000_000 `surrender value` NOTHING `debts` NOTHING `medical costs` NOTHING) EQUALS `the temporary cover benefit` 100_000_000

§§ `F-10, F-11, F-12 — the summary notes against the Rules and Terms`

-- F-10: three options and no criterion in the notes; one consequence per case in 12.2(a).
#ASSERT count `notes item 1 — the options open to Prudential on a misdeclaration` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `Article 12.2(a) — the consequence of a misdeclaration` TRUE EQUALS `the contract or the reinstatement is cancelled; no benefit is paid and no premium is refunded`
-- F-11: suicide. The notes exclude every benefit for an event "related to" suicide; the Rules
-- and Terms pay 8.7 (30m), because a suicide is no Accident and 11.1 reaches only 8.1-8.6.
#ASSERT `notes item 3 — excluded` `the policy` (`suicide or self-injury, linked as` `directly caused by it`) (YMD 2027 3 20) (YMD 2027 3 20) FALSE
#ASSERT `the death claim` `the policy` (`a death on` (YMD 2027 3 20) `from` NOTHING `as` `any other circumstance`) `the accounts` `nothing paid yet` EQUALS `the non-accidental death benefit, Article 8.7` 30_000_000
-- F-11: a crime no State authority has concluded: excluded in the notes, not in 11.1(b).
#ASSERT `notes item 3 — excluded` `the policy` (`a crime, linked as` `directly caused by it` `concluded by an authority` FALSE) (YMD 2027 3 10) (YMD 2027 3 10) FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 8.4 — the fracture benefit` `the policy` (`an accident on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `with` (`a crime, linked as` `directly caused by it` `concluded by an authority` FALSE)) (LIST `a fracture of` `a rib` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `previously broken` NOTHING) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 100_000_000
-- F-11: a cause that is only related, not the direct cause: excluded in the notes, not in 11.1.
#ASSERT `notes item 3 — excluded` `the policy` (`a dangerous activity, linked as` `related to it, but not caused by it`) (YMD 2027 3 10) (YMD 2027 3 10) FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 8.4 — the fracture benefit` `the policy` (`an accident on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `with` (`a dangerous activity, linked as` `related to it, but not caused by it`)) (LIST `a fracture of` `a rib` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `previously broken` NOTHING) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 100_000_000
-- F-12: a 10-year-old's fracture cap, sum insured 1bn: the notes say the lesser of 100% and
-- 500m (500m); Article 8.4 says the lesser of 100% and 250m (250m).
#ASSERT `notes item 2 — the fracture maximum over the term` (`the same policy for` 1_000_000_000 `on an insured born` (YMD 2016 6 1)) EQUALS 500_000_000
#ASSERT `the term cap for fractures and burns, for` (`the same policy for` 1_000_000_000 `on an insured born` (YMD 2016 6 1)) `at an event on` (YMD 2027 3 10) EQUALS 250_000_000
-- F-12: burns, the same.
#ASSERT `notes item 2 — the burn maximum over the term` (`the same policy for` 1_000_000_000 `on an insured born` (YMD 2016 6 1)) EQUALS 500_000_000
-- F-12: ambulance. The notes give 2m a contract year and nothing per Accident; Article 8.6 pays
-- 1m an Accident, so one Accident never reaches the 2m the notes print.
#ASSERT `notes item 2 — the ambulance maximum per contract year` EQUALS 2_000_000
#ASSERT `Article 8.6 — the ambulance benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (`treated overnight in` (JUST (`an intensive care unit in` (`a facility of kind` `a hospital`) `which is an emergency room` FALSE)) `transferred` TRUE) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 1_000_000
-- Where they agree: the accidental death maximum (300%), the maturity rates, the surrender value.
#ASSERT `notes item 2 — the most the accidental death benefit pays` `the policy` EQUALS 3_000_000_000
#ASSERT `notes item 2 — the maturity gift for a term in years of` 10 `with` `the accounts` EQUALS 22_500_000
#ASSERT `notes item 4 — the contract has a surrender value` `the policy` TRUE `on` (YMD 2028 1 15) EQUALS `Article 1.13 — the contract has a surrender value` `the policy` TRUE `on` (YMD 2028 1 15)
#ASSERT REFUSED `notes item 2 — the maturity gift for a term in years of` 7 `with` `the accounts` BECAUSE "the summary notes state no maturity rate for this term"

§§ `F-13 — who receives`

-- An individual policyholder who has died, and a sole beneficiary who died before the insured
-- event: no limb of 10.8.2 names anyone.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 10.8 — who receives the benefit` `death caused by an Accident (10.3)` (`an adult resident born` (YMD 1980 1 1)) FALSE FALSE (LIST `beneficiary` "A" `share` 100 `alive` FALSE `harmed the insured` FALSE) BECAUSE "Article 10.8 names no recipient who can take in this case"
-- A company's policy, the insured alive and injured: the fracture benefit goes to the
-- beneficiary the company named, or with none named, to the company; never to the insured.
#ASSERT `Article 10.8 — who receives the benefit` `permanent injury, internal organ injury, fracture or burn caused by an Accident (10.4)` `a company` TRUE TRUE (LIST `beneficiary` "the insured's spouse" `share` 100 `alive` TRUE `harmed the insured` FALSE) EQUALS LIST `the designated beneficiary` "the insured's spouse"
#ASSERT `Article 10.8 — who receives the benefit` `permanent injury, internal organ injury, fracture or burn caused by an Accident (10.4)` `a company` TRUE TRUE EMPTY EQUALS LIST `the policyholder as recipient`

§§ `F-14 — discretion with no criterion`

-- Article 9: notice of a new occupation one day late opens the power to decline ANY later
-- claim; the rule does not look at the claim at all.
#ASSERT `Article 9 — Prudential may decline to pay a claim` (`The occupation history` OF JUST (YMD 2027 1 1), JUST (YMD 2027 2 1), FALSE, NOTHING) (YMD 1990 6 1)
#ASSERT count `Article 9 — the options open to Prudential on a notified change` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT count (`Article 12.2(d) — the options open to Prudential` FALSE) EQUALS 3

§§ `F-15 — incontestability protects against nothing that cancels`

-- A material misstatement may be raised in year 9 (Article 6), and its consequence is
-- cancellation with no refund (12.2(a)); a misstatement that is not material could only ever
-- bring extra premium, and that is all Article 6 shuts off after 24 months.
#ASSERT `Article 6 — Prudential may still raise the misstatement` `the policy` (`A misstatement` OF TRUE, YMD 2034 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 6 — Prudential may still raise the misstatement` `the policy` (`A misstatement` OF FALSE, YMD 2034 6 1)

§§ `F-16 — a reinstatement asked for in time, defeated by Prudential's own delay`

-- Lapsed 2027-01-01; request 2028-12-20 (in time); confirmation letter 2029-01-05. By then the
-- lapse exceeds 24 months (Article 16), so the reinstatement never takes effect.
#ASSERT `Article 12.1(h) — the request may be made` `the policy` (`A reinstatement request` OF YMD 2027 1 1, YMD 2028 12 20, TRUE, TRUE, JUST (YMD 2029 1 5), TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `Article 12.1(h) — the date the reinstatement takes effect` `the policy` (`A reinstatement request` OF YMD 2027 1 1, YMD 2028 12 20, TRUE, TRUE, JUST (YMD 2029 1 5), TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
